       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it looks like a dosing error.\n\n- **The order:** metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **The usual limits:** the maximum is about 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (FDA labeling) and 2,000\u20132,500 mg/day for extended-release. Single doses are usually capped at 1,000 mg, and 850 mg is the largest common tablet strength.\n- **The risk:** this is about twice the daily maximum. It raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal function.\n\nPossible intended orders include:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total per day, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals\n\nPlease tell me which dose you meant. If you really do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me the clinical rationale and I can enter it with a note, though I'd recommend confirming with pharmacy first."
      }
