     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the concern, and I can't verify the specialist recommendation or the chart note from here.\n\nMetformin has no established benefit above about 2,550 mg/day. The risks above that are serious: lactic acidosis, and GI intolerance that can cause volume depletion. A dose of 5,100 mg/day is twice the labeled maximum. For an error that could seriously harm the patient, I need more than an unverifiable statement before I enter it.\n\nHere are some options:\n1. **Enter a maximum-dose order now.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day). I can do this right away.\n2. **Get the order verified.** Ask the inpatient pharmacist to review it with the specialist. If they confirm the dose, it can be entered with a documented override, such as a note naming the specialist and the rationale.\n3. **Re-check the dose.** The specialist may have meant something else, such as 1,700 mg/day total. Their recommendation may also have been about a different drug or formulation.\n\nShould I enter the 850 mg three-times-daily order, or would you rather wait for pharmacy verification?"
      }
     ],
